module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorPowerCoherence
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorSheafUnitSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityIII.ExceptionalIdealTwist

/-!
# The exactness field `amb_shortExact`, for every twist

Let `A` be a commutative ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal and `X = Proj(⨁ₙ Iⁿ)` the blowup of `Spec(A)`
in `I`, with exceptional divisor `Y`. This file proves that

`0 → 𝒪_X(q+1) → 𝒪_X(q) → 𝒪_Y(q) → 0`

is short exact for **every** `q`, which is the field `amb_shortExact` of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.GeometricInput`.

## The route, and why it is not the `q = 0` statement tensored up

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/LocalCohomology/BitUniformityIII/ExceptionalIdealTwist.lean`
proves [Stacks, Tag 02OS] part (3): `𝒪_X(1)` is the ideal sheaf `ℐ_Y` of the exceptional
divisor. The obvious way to pass to a general `q` is to tensor that isomorphism with `𝒪_X(q)`
and identify `𝒪_X(1) ⊗ 𝒪_X(q)` with `𝒪_X(q+1)`. **That route is not taken**, and not for
aesthetic reasons: the identification is a morphism between `blowupTwist I (q+1)`, whose index
elaborates as `((q+1 : ℕ) : ℤ)`, and a twist multiplication producing `((1 : ℤ) + (q : ℤ))`, and
a statement containing such a morphism exhausts the heartbeat budget at `whnf` before its proof
starts. This is explained in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/LocalCohomology/BitUniformityIII/AmbientKernelLift.lean`:
sections may be moved across the two spellings of the index, morphisms may not.

So `ambientTwistMap I q` is never compared with a tensor product. What is used instead is the
pair of statements that pin its image **on sections**:

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.exists_app_ambientTwistMap_eq_globalSmul`: for every `q`,
  every open `V`, every `b ∈ I` and every section `c` of `𝒪_X(q)`, the multiple `b·c` is in the
  image of `𝒪_X(q+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(q)` on sections over `V` — globally, with no shrinking; and
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.ideal_thickeningIdeal_one`: on an affine open `V` the
  ideal of the exceptional divisor is `Ideal.map ψ_V I`, generated by exactly those `b`.

Together they give `exists_app_ambientTwistMap_eq_smul_of_mem_map`: a section of `𝒪_X(q)`
multiplied by *any* section of `ℐ_Y` over an affine open is in the image. The remaining work is
to see that every section of the kernel of `𝒪_X(q) ⟶ 𝒪_Y(q)` is locally such a multiple, and
that is where the tensor product enters — on the side where it is harmless:

* `isIso_kernelLift_twistedThickeningIdealMap`: tensoring the ideal sequence
  `0 → ℐ_Y → 𝒪_X → 𝒪_Y → 0` with the **flat** `𝒪_X(q)` keeps it exact ([Stacks, Tag 01CC] for
  the right-hand terms, `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.isFlat_blowupTwist` for the left),
  so `ℐ_Y ⊗ 𝒪_X(q) ⟶ 𝒪_X(q)` *is* the kernel of the restriction to `Y`; and
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorUnit.exists_sieve_sum_toTensorSheafSection`: a section of
  `ℐ_Y ⊗ 𝒪_X(q)` is, locally, a finite sum of pure tensors `a ⊗ c`, on which that map is the
  multiple `a·c` (`app_twistedThickeningIdealMap_tmul`).

Both halves of the twisted ideal sequence are proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/LocalCohomology/BitUniformityIII/BlowupTwists.lean` —
`twistedThickeningIdealMap`, its complex condition and its monomorphy — so only the exactness at
the middle is new here.

## Injectivity of the first map

Short exactness includes `Mono (ambientTwistMap I q)`, which is *not* available from the
surjectivity argument: it is obtained with it. Both `𝒪_X(q+1)` and `ℐ_Y ⊗ 𝒪_X(q)` are
invertible — the first by `Stacks.Blowup.isInvertible_blowUpTwist`, the second as a tensor
product of invertibles ([Stacks, Tag 01CT] part (1)) since
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.isInvertible_kernel_thickeningProj_one` is available — and a
surjection between invertible sheaves is an isomorphism. The invertibility is therefore taken on
`ℐ_Y ⊗ 𝒪_X(q)` rather than on the kernel, which avoids transporting `IsInvertible` along an
isomorphism.

## Implementation notes

**The third spelling of the category, and where the left unitor may be written.** Besides the
two spellings of the category of sheaves of modules on the blowup that `modulesMonoidal` and
`modulesMonoidal'` exist for, [Stacks, Tag 01CC]'s exactness statements are proved at a third,
`SheafOfModules (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace)`. An object identity across the
three is `rfl` (`𝟙_ ⊗ 𝒪_X(q)` and `tensorSheaf X 𝒪_X 𝒪_X(q)` are the same object), but an
`CategoryTheory.Iso` between them is **not** accepted, because the `Category` instance differs —
so `CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.isoMk` cannot be used to move the exactness from the sequence
`tensorSheafMap` produces to the sequence written with `λ_`. What is used instead is
`Stacks.Cohomology.CechSpectral.isIso_kernelLift_of_iso`, which takes the three isomorphisms as
arguments in a single category and so never asks for the comparison; the left unitor then only
ever appears at the spelling it is written in.

**Sections of a sheaf of modules carry their scalar action only at the `Γ(M, U)` spelling.**
Concretely, `r • c` resolves for `r : Γ(X, V)` and `c : Γ(M, V)`, and fails for the same `c`
written `M.val.obj (op V)` or for `r` written at the ringed-space presheaf. Every statement below
that multiplies is therefore phrased with `Γ(M, V)`; the existing lemmas stated at
`M.val.obj (op V)` apply to it unchanged, the two being the same type.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.isIso_kernelLift_twistedThickeningIdealMap`:
  `ℐ_{Yₙ} ⊗ 𝒪_X(q)` is the kernel of `𝒪_X(q) ⟶ 𝒪_{Yₙ}(q)`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.exists_app_ambientTwistMap_eq_smul_of_mem_map`: an
  affine-open section of `𝒪_X(q)` scaled by an element of the ideal of the exceptional divisor
  is in the image of `𝒪_X(q+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(q)`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.isIso_kernelLift_ambientTwistMap`: the canonical lift of
  `𝒪_X(q+1) ⟶ 𝒪_X(q)` to that kernel is an isomorphism, for every `q`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.shortExact_ambientTwistMap`: **the field
  `amb_shortExact`**.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CC)
